<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Duchess Elizabeth Feodorovna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Elisabeth of Hesse and by Rhine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grand Duchess Elizabeth Feodorovna, born Princess Elisabeth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>, was a daughter of Grand Duke Louis IV and Princess Alice. In 1884 she married Grand Duke Sergei Alexandrovich of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and after his assassination in 1905 she founded a religious community of nursing sisters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. She was killed by the Bolsheviks at Alapayevsk in 1918 and has been canonised as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-duchess-elizabeth-feodorovna.jpg" alt="Grand Duchess Elizabeth Feodorovna" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Bergamasco · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Duchess_Elisabeth_Fedorovna_in_1885.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
